<article class="env-lemma" id="0GBS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GBS">Lemma <span data-tag="0GBS">87.23.1</span>.</a> Let $A$ and $B$ be pre-adic topological rings. Let $\varphi : A \to B$ be a continuous ring homomorphism. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $\varphi $ is adic, then $\varphi $ is taut. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $B$ is complete, $A$ has a finitely generated ideal of definition, and $\varphi $ is taut, then $\varphi $ is adic. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> In particular the conditions “$\varphi $ is adic” and “$\varphi $ is taut” are equivalent on the category $\textit{WAdm}^{adic*}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Part (1) is Lemma <a href="/tag/0GXC" data-tag="0GXC">87.6.4</a>. Part (2) is Lemma <a href="/tag/0APU" data-tag="0APU">87.6.5</a>. The final statement is a consequence of (1) and (2). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>